think Read the wave docs (1024-round itinerary, six-season double-seat, rye-first crypto-parity decision wave) and the crypto front doors. Season G crypto is the high-Lindy live thread; the identity arc's carry (kumara_carry) closed as the eighteenth composition. Both the carry log and the REMEMBER git nib named the same next door outright: a per-record subkey carry (a hardened child of the identity node).
think Lindy-first crux-first: the subkey is the intended next crux and higher-Lindy than the alternative BIP-49/84 wallet paths — the Identity struct was DELIBERATELY given a chain_code field with the comment "so a caller can derive further children (a per-record subkey) without re-walking from the seed." The groundwork was laid; this rung reads that chain code and steps one level deeper. It serves the provenance spine (Season 2 Journey 6, Lotus): one identity signing many records without spending the same signing key on each.
think Read kumara_identity, kumara_carry, kumara_path, and slip10_ed25519's Node/ckd_priv API. A subkey is the hardened child m/44'/coin'/account'/index'/record' of the identity node. Reconstruct the parent node from the Identity (key = secret_seed, chain_code = chain_code, depth = 4, the Kumara path's fixed depth), ckd_priv with record+hardened_offset, read the child's public key the same two independent ways the identity door does. Confirmed the current edge (kumara_carry) GREEN on metal before composing (measurement before narrative).
think Authored crypto/kumara_subkey.rye authoring NO new cryptography and NO new frame: derive_subkey (postcondition asserts the child sits one depth below the identity and the two public derivations agree), subkey_from_mnemonic (the one-call phrase→identity→subkey arc), sign/verify thin wrappers, seal_as (signed_carry under the subkey's seed), open_as (reuses kumara_carry's binding — it takes a raw public key, so no duplication of the UnexpectedSigner logic). TAME: opening triad, u32 widths, named errors, invariants >=2 per fn with // invariant:, record level bounded below 2^31, snake_case, no @memcpy.
obs One honest boundary named as the next rung: ed25519/SLIP-0010 admits only hardened derivation, so a subkey's public key CANNOT be derived from the parent's public alone — a verifier holding only the identity's public key cannot on their own prove a subkey descends from it. The parent->subkey attestation (the identity SIGNING a "this subkey is mine at record r" statement, a signed delegation over exactly the kumara_carry door) is the named next rung. This rung proves what stands beneath: deterministic per-record separation, each subkey a real working signing key, each subkey sealing/opening as itself with the wrong-key binding refused.
obs Proof shape, three replayable ways with no fabricated constant: (1) anchored to the identity arc — the subkey at record r equals walking ckd_priv from the same identity node by hand, its public key equal to both slip10's public form 0x00-tag-stripped and ed25519_sign's independent derive_public; (2) separation — same identity+record -> identical subkey, a different record -> a different subkey, every subkey differs from its parent identity; (3) a real working signing key — signs a message verify accepts, a flipped message byte and a flipped signature byte refuse, and it seals a record open_as verifies as the subkey while refusing the parent identity and a sibling subkey with UnexpectedSigner across six payload lengths; a record at the hardened offset refuses NotHardened. GREEN on the first metal pass.
obs Registered the witness in crypto_suite_witness (after kumara_carry) and bumped the authoritative counts 53->54 files, 18->19 compositions in the suite header + final line, crypto/README.md (heading, witness count, new composition row), and docs/CRYPTO.md (subtitle, rung-table heading, witness count, new rung row). Count guard GREEN at 54 (bijection: every crypto/*.rye registered, every registration a real file). TAME style bans clean.
